        {
          "unit_id": "the_reviews",
          "title": "The Reviews",
          "description": "Habla como la prensa: it is said that…, he is believed to…, they are expected to… Además, adverbios que dan tu opinión: apparently, clearly, surprisingly, fortunately.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "the_reviews_lesson",
              "title": "Passive reporting structures",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The reviews",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Listen to this: \"The Clifton Cats' first album is said to be the surprise of the year.\""
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "The surprise of the year! Sam must be over the moon."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "There's more. \"The band is believed to have signed a deal for a European tour.\""
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "A European tour? Is it true?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "It's being reported everywhere. Apparently they're expected to play in Madrid in June."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Madrid! We have to go. Javi could fly from Dublin."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "What else does it say?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "\"The singer, Sam Turner, is thought to have written most of the songs in a small house in Bristol.\""
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "That's our house! Our kitchen is famous."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Ollie",
                        "text": "It's also well known that he never cleaned it."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Priya",
                        "text": "Ha! It says the album was recorded in just six weeks."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Let's call him. He's supposed to be in London this week."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "March. Sam's album is out, and Priya is reading the reviews aloud in the kitchen."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"The album is said to be the surprise of the year.\" means…",
                        "options": [
                          "people say it is",
                          "the album says it"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"The band is believed to have signed a deal.\" To have signed refers to…",
                        "options": [
                          "the past",
                          "the future"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"It's being reported everywhere.\" The tense is…",
                        "options": [
                          "present continuous passive",
                          "present perfect passive"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Where are they expected to play in June?",
                        "options": [
                          "Madrid",
                          "Bristol",
                          "Dublin"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "passive_reporting",
                    "title": "Passive reporting structures",
                    "explanation": "En noticias y textos formales contamos lo que dice la gente sin decir quién:\n• It is said / believed / thought / expected that + frase: It is said that the album is the surprise of the year.\n• Sujeto + is said / believed / thought / expected + to + verbo: The album is said to be the surprise of the year.\n• Si se refiere al pasado, to have + participio: The band is believed to have signed a deal.\n\nBe supposed to significa «se supone que»: He's supposed to be in London this week.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "It is said that…",
                          "It is said that the album is the surprise of the year."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Sujeto + is said to + verbo",
                          "The album is said to be the surprise of the year."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Sujeto + is believed to have + participio (pasado)",
                          "The band is believed to have signed a deal."
                        ],
                        [
                          "be expected to",
                          "They're expected to play in Madrid."
                        ],
                        [
                          "be supposed to",
                          "He's supposed to be in London this week."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "The Clifton Cats' first album is said to be the surprise of the year.",
                      "The band is believed to have signed a deal for a European tour.",
                      "Apparently they're expected to play in Madrid in June.",
                      "He's supposed to be in London this week."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "attitudinal_adverbs",
                    "title": "Attitudinal adverbs: apparently, clearly, fortunately",
                    "explanation": "Algunos adverbios no dicen cómo se hace algo, sino qué opinamos de toda la frase. Suelen ir al principio, seguidos de coma:\n\n• Apparently (según parece, por lo visto): Apparently, they're playing in Madrid. Ojo: no significa «aparentemente» en el sentido de «a simple vista»; se usa para información que nos han contado.\n• Clearly / Obviously (está claro que): Clearly, the critics love the album.\n• Surprisingly / Not surprisingly: Surprisingly, it was recorded in six weeks.\n• Fortunately / Luckily ≠ Unfortunately: Unfortunately, the tour doesn't come to Bristol.\n• Honestly / Frankly (sinceramente): Frankly, I never liked their old songs.\n• Hopefully (ojalá, con suerte): Hopefully, we'll get tickets.\n\nTambién pueden ir en medio: The band has clearly worked very hard.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Adverbio",
                        "Ejemplo",
                        "En español"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "apparently",
                          "Apparently, they're touring Europe.",
                          "por lo visto"
                        ],
                        [
                          "clearly / obviously",
                          "Clearly, the critics love it.",
                          "está claro que"
                        ],
                        [
                          "surprisingly",
                          "Surprisingly, it took six weeks.",
                          "sorprendentemente"
                        ],
                        [
                          "fortunately / unfortunately",
                          "Unfortunately, it's sold out.",
                          "por suerte / por desgracia"
                        ],
                        [
                          "hopefully",
                          "Hopefully, we'll get tickets.",
                          "con suerte"
                        ],
                        [
                          "frankly",
                          "Frankly, the cover is ugly.",
                          "francamente"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Apparently, the band is playing in Madrid in June.",
                      "Clearly, Sam has worked very hard on this album.",
                      "Surprisingly, the album was recorded in just six weeks.",
                      "Unfortunately, the Madrid concert is already sold out."
                    ]
                  }
                },
